{
  "about": "EXP-008 parity fixture: rust-live (crates/strategies/src/scenario_executor.rs) and the bridge (bridge_py/tests/test_scenario.py) must turn every case into exactly these tranches. `tranches` is the pure sizing rule (position, target -> side, qty, reduces). In `cases` each executor is built once from `config` (missing keys take the ScenarioCfg defaults) and `max_order_notional_frac` (the [risk] per-order cap; null = no clamp), then runs every step in order, so pacing memory carries across steps. Per step: books are YES-space [best bid, best ask] pips (a null side is empty, a null book is missing), `stale` books are older than the freshness limit, `live_intent` means a scenario order is already working there, `targets` null means no target file, and `increase_allowed` false means the target file is stale or invalid. `expect` lists the orders in emission order (side-relative limit pips); every `notes` entry must be a substring of some note of that decision.",
